{"repositoryId":1414510815,"availability":"available","full":"mastro993/lucca-traffic-twin","name":"lucca-traffic-twin","description":"3D, hour-by-hour SUMO microsimulation of traffic in Lucca (Italy): OSM network, calibrated demand, critical junctions, deck.gl viewer","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-11T15:56:35Z","updated":"2026-10-16T10:07:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://mastro993.github.io/lucca-traffic-twin/","topics":["deckgl","digital-twin","italy","lucca","mobility","openstreetmap","sumo","traffic-simulation"],"demo":"https://mastro993.github.io/lucca-traffic-twin/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T00:42:13.118Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T00:42:13.118Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T00:42:13.118Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T19:08:56.394Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-19T00:42:13.118Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A 3D, hour-by-hour microsimulation of road traffic in Lucca (Italy) and the surrounding plain, built with Eclipse SUMO on the real OpenStreetMap network. It simulates a typical school weekday and a Saturday, 24 hours each, and ranks the junctions where traffic loses the most time.","The goal is a calibrated baseline for testing how traffic in Lucca could be improved: junction redesigns, new links, signal timing, school-time staggering, parking policy. Every vehicle (about 340,000 trips on a weekday) is simulated individually.","This is a model, not a live traffic feed. The demand is synthetic and calibrated to the few public traffic counts available (see Calibration and Limits). Rely on the ranking of critical points more than on the absolute delays."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mastro993/lucca-traffic-twin/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e89f1b65e513c03bb46710607cf0d08acb7bfda37d81a4b9b4ca84c9422354c5","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T19:08:56.524Z"},"